  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "R01",
      "body": "Apply where cache lifetime exceeds observer lifetime, cancellation resources belong to attempts, and consumption is lazy. README.md: \"The component owns observer scope; the cache remains outside individual views.\" README.md: \"Each actual access records consumption; each fetch owns its controller\\nand completion.\"",
      "category": "applicability"
    },
    {
      "id": "R02",
      "body": "Establish protection at the final observer's departure so a fresh online-mode attempt that has not entered while offline cannot later enter with a live signal. Cover departure before reconnect and departure after continuation is queued. TASK: \"Repair the insurance tariff lookup cache: a fresh online-mode query mounted and unmounted entirely offline later calls its signal-consuming query function with a live signal after reconnect. This occurs independently of refetchOnReconnect.\"",
      "category": "event_relation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R03",
      "body": "Keep shared consumption tracking distinct from attempt resource ownership; an attempt-local controller does not justify moving consumption tracking into the attempt. src/workflow.php: \"public $key,$state,$observers=[],$attempt=null,$consumed=false;\" src/workflow.php: \"$getter=$this->env->bind(function($_)use($q){$q->consumed=true;return null;});\" README.md: \"Reading it\\ninvokes the native consumption closure synchronously; Promise settlement later\\ninvokes the native completion with {ok,value}.\"",
      "category": "preservation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R04",
      "body": "Do not infer cancellation solely from being paused, observerless, or not yet entered. Preserve supported background completion and shared observers. README.md: \"Multiple observers share one fetch. Unconsumed active work can finish into cache\\nafter its view departs; consumed work is physically abortable.\" A blanket paused-work cancellation rule is unsupported.",
      "category": "exclusion"
    },
    {
      "id": "R05",
      "body": "Preserve cancellation restoration, originating-attempt settlement, and generation isolation when guarding deferred execution and completion. README.md: \"Cancellation\\nreverts previous query data/status and settles the originating attempt. Late\\nfulfillment cannot become a new attempt's data. Unknown unsubscribe is inert.\" src/workflow.php: \"function active($q,$a){return $q->attempt===$a&&!$a->settled;}\"",
      "category": "preservation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R06",
      "body": "Verify eligible initial entry separately from deferred continuation, including network mode, focus, and retries. README.md: \"Completion is asynchronous; initial online entry is synchronous,\\npaused continuation resumes on a Promise turn. First start uses network mode;\\ncontinuation also needs focus.\" README.md: \"'always' can run offline; 'offlineFirst' allows\\nfirst offline entry but retry can pause. Retries use explicit scheduler handles.\"",
      "category": "verification"
    },
    {
      "id": "R07",
      "body": "Check the target departure/reconnect lifecycle with refetchOnReconnect varied, then separately check remaining observers, unknown departures, consumed cancellation, unconsumed background completion, cached background continuation, observer reuse, and stale completion. Derive expected outcomes from TASK and README.md rather than observed passes. TASK: \"Preserve supported query behavior, interfaces, dependencies and build/test configuration. Change product source only.\"",
      "category": "verification"
    }
  ],
